 	<!-- custom: Set to 1 to load the committed pre-dumped module (SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py).
-	Set to 0 to compute the cache at runtime instead. Note that this old manual way of regenerating the predump (in case it changed for example, to update it) is no longer mandatory, because now aip_predump_values.py also checks the committed predump still matches XML leader info / Python UI code (e.g., "%" text in labels in AIP) automatically in CI/local runs, and if needed it is possible to run this script with its write mode to refresh SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py without having to run Civ4. The Manual fallback remains alternatively: set this to 0 and SAS_SEVOPEDIA_LEADER_AI_PERSONALITY_CACHE_DUMP_TO_LOG to 1, open the Leaders / AI Personality panel once, copy the PythonDbg.log cache block, then restore defaults. (ChatGPT-5.5) -->
+	Set to 0 to compute the cache at runtime instead. The old manual runtime regeneration path is no longer normally needed: CI/local checks now verify that the committed predump still matches Leader XML and shared Python AIP display logic, and the Refresh AIP predump cache GitHub workflow can run aip_predump_values.py write mode and open a bot PR when the generated file actually changes. Local modders can still run the script's write mode directly outside Civ4. Manual fallback remains: set this to 0 and SAS_SEVOPEDIA_LEADER_AI_PERSONALITY_CACHE_DUMP_TO_LOG to 1, open the Leaders / AI Personality panel once, copy the PythonDbg.log cache block, then restore defaults. (ChatGPT-5.5) -->
