-Set to 0 if you always want to compute despite it being more costly (for modding, etc.), but don't always want to dump to log as this needlessly crowds the log and is expensive if done every time. Recommended settings: if SAS_SEVOPEDIA_LEADER_AI_PERSONALITY_CACHE_USE_PREDUMPED is set to 1, the value of SAS_SEVOPEDIA_LEADER_AI_PERSONALITY_CACHE_DUMP_TO_LOG here won't matter and is not used (we don't dump to log at all regardless), else if SAS_SEVOPEDIA_LEADER_AI_PERSONALITY_CACHE_USE_PREDUMPED is set to 0, set this SAS_SEVOPEDIA_LEADER_AI_PERSONALITY_CACHE_DUMP_TO_LOG temporarily to 1 so you can get from dbg log to update the cachepredumped py file, then you can disable it as no need to crowd your log with all this dmp and less expensive as such.
